WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.267
A test suite is a group of tests.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:07.692
In real projects, tests are often stored in separate files and run with testing tools.

00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:13.002
But the idea is the same as what we see here.

00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:16.112
We have a function called normalize_status.

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:20.412
This version also replaces spaces with underscores.

00:00:20.412 --> 00:00:23.572
Then we define two test functions.

00:00:23.572 --> 00:00:25.972
The first test checks the complete status.

00:00:25.972 --> 00:00:28.707
The second checks In Progress and expects in_progress.

00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:34.407
At the bottom, we loop through the test functions and run each one.

00:00:34.407 --> 00:00:37.807
If both tests pass, the program prints All tests passed.

00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:44.517
This structure may look simple, but it introduces an important habit.

00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:51.082
Instead of manually checking output every time, we write small checks that Python can run for us.

00:00:51.082 --> 00:00:54.240
That gives us confidence when we revise code later.
